# LifePunch — Quality Bar (No Spaghetti)

This repo is a **reference** others will copy, and it will get much larger. Quality and
security beat speed. We take the time; that is what players recognize. Maintain this across
ALL of LifePunch (weapons, entities, website, code) — not just the current task.

## What counts as spaghetti / hacky (AVOID)
- Fighting the engine's intended system instead of using it (invisible materials to hide a
  master mesh, "passenger" renderers, raw `.vmdl` `base_model_name` hacks, hidden masters).
- Dead/disabled components or orphaned assets left in files "just in case".
- Workarounds stacked on workarounds; anything you'd be embarrassed to have copied.
- One-off fixes that don't generalize to the next weapon/entity of the same class.

## The clean alternative
- Use the system as designed (e.g. a real viewmodel rig with a `camera` bone + animgraph;
  config over forked systems; one class template reused as data).
- Prefer the fully-owned solution over one that depends on a third party shipping something.

## Mandatory: flag it, don't bury it
1. **Call it out the moment it appears.** If a step needs a hack, say so explicitly and
   label it temporary — never present a hack as "done".
2. **Offer the clean path** (even if slower) and let the user choose clean-now vs. interim.
3. **If an interim is accepted, TRACK it** in `lifepunch/addons/docs/TECH_DEBT.md` with:
   what's temporary, why, the clean endgame, and the single swap point to fix it.
   A placeholder must never silently become permanent.

## Examples from this project
- ❌ vm_ak47 invisible-M4-master + bonemerged static AK + 3rd "passenger" renderer → empty
  hands. Spaghetti.
- ⚠️ vm_ak47 running the real M4 viewmodel as an honest, labeled **placeholder** → clean
  *only if* tracked in TECH_DEBT.md and the AK passenger/orphan assets are removed.
- ✅ Endgame: own a per-class viewmodel rig (camera bone + animgraph) and skin each weapon
  mesh to it — no dependency on Facepunch shipping source.
